{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "The UML is not Sufficient"}, {"type": "position", "content": 1}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear and use when you talk about the Unified Modeling Language."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe common activities at work to a visitor using short sentences in familiar spoken and written situations.  Give detailed information related to UML and common related topics."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations.  Describes common activities related to Software Programming through the use of appropriate expressions, grammar and vocabulary in written or spoken situations according to the abilities related to this level."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe7n4le02ob01re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "currently "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "at the moment, now, at present"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'm currently planning to create a piece of business software, but I'm still trying to find a suitable modeling technique."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n4le02ob01aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "shortcoming "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "disadvantage, limitation or deficiency"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: That's exactly what I wanted to tell you, in my company we realized that UML is great, but it has shortcomings."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n4le02ob01aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "semantics "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the study of meaning in structured language"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I had a colleague who tried to use her own modeling, but it created some difficulties in semantics because it wasn't like ours, so we had to \u201ctranslate\u201d what she meant."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n4le02ob01aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "impair"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to damage, to harm or to spoil"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Dealing with other important elements in a different order might impair the process."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n4le02ob01aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "purpose"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "objective, goal or aim"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Some friends told me they were doing that in theirs too, when it's clearly not its purpose."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n4le02ob01aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "proprietary model"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a personal or customized model"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun): "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There are so many UML models that it'd be difficult to see all of them in one single software; it would also have to support proprietary models. It's too complex!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n4le02ob01aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Research on other representation method for specific purposes."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write examples of why to use that method instead of UML using the present continuous. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share with my partners. "}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I talk about the functionalities of different languages besidesUML. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write about why to use another method in present continuous."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share my findings with my partners."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Present Continuous (Review)"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use the <strong>present continuous tense</strong> to talk about actions that happen at the moment of speaking or for future plans."}, {"type": "text", "content": "If you want to say that something is happening right now, or at the time of speaking, you use the <strong>present continuous</strong>, follow this structure to make affirmative sentences: </br></br>  <div class=\"center_text\"> Subject+ verb to be (am/is/are) + verb (-ing form) + complement</div></br></br>  Examples: </br>  I'<strong>m trying </strong>to find other alternatives apart from UML. </br> We'<strong>re working </strong>on new modeling languages. </br>  If you want to make negative sentences you can use this structure: </br></br> <div class=\"center_text\"> Subject + verb to be (am/is/are) + not + verb (-ing form) + complement</div></br></br>  Examples: </br> She'<strong>s not following </strong>the modeling scheme! </br> They'<strong>re not making progress </strong>on the software. </br></br>  The structure changes a little when making questions in present continuous; here's the structure: </br></br>  <div class=\"center_text\"> verb to be (am/is/are) + subject + verb (-ing form) + complement + ? </div></br></br>  Examples: </br>  <strong>Are</strong> you <strong>using </strong>the modeling scheme we proposed? </br> <strong>Is</strong> UML <strong>providing</strong> you with the necessary tools?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Well, I'm currently planning to create a piece of business software, but I'm still trying to find a suitable modeling technique."}, {"type": "example", "content": "In mine, we're still following it thoroughly, but in this case it's not working."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Possessive Pronouns"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use <strong>Possessive pronouns </strong>to make reference to something that you mentioned previously, they help you avoid repetition of possessions, thus improving your fluency."}, {"type": "text", "content": "These pronouns help you to refer to and object that belongs to someone, but the speaker mentioned it before in the conversation. </br></br>  Example: </br></br>  <strong>John</strong>: My company doesn't use the UML. </br> <strong>Danny</strong>: That's strange. <strong>Mine </strong>loves it! </br></br>  Danny talks about his Company, but he does not repeat the word Company because John used it before. </br></br>  The purpose of these pronouns is to avoid repetition of concepts that both speakers know about. </br></br>  Example: </br></br>  I know they use very efficient models, but <strong>ours </strong>are more object oriented. </br></br>  Remember, possessive adjectives and different and ALWAYS require you to use the object you possess. But possessive pronouns do not. </br></br>  Example: </br> <strong>His </strong>diagram looks messy, but <strike> my  </strike>is better. (Incorrect) </br> His diagram looks messy, but <strong>mine</strong> is better. (Correct) </br>  Here is a list of both possessives (adjectives and pronouns):"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":8,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Possessive adjectives\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Possessive pronouns\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"My\\t\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Mine\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Your\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Yours\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"His\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"His\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Her\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Hers\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Its\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Its\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Our\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Ours\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Their\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Theirs\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Words Endings \"ant - ent\""}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Sometimes these word endings might cause confusions because both word endings can be used in adjectives and nouns. However, if you pay close attention to them, you will be all right!  "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You need to be careful with the spelling because sometimes the pronunciation might appear to be the same but the words are written differently. In the box below, you will find some of the most common words that end in Ent or Ant, particularly nouns and adjectives."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":7,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Ant\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Ent\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adjectives\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Nouns\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adjectives\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Nouns\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Constant\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Accountant\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Absent \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Accident\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Dominant\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Consultant\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Coherent\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Component\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Elegant\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Stimulant \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Evident\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Document\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Important\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Stimulant\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Imminent\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Parent\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Significant\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Defendant\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Permanent\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Recipient\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "So creativity or dealing with other important elements in a different order might impair the process."}], "type": "learning_points"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "100", "image": "enpe7n4le02ob01re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<strong>Michelle</strong>: I see that you really enjoy doing models with UML, right? </br>\n<strong>Jack</strong>: Well, I'm currently planning to create a piece of business software, but I'm still trying to find a suitable modeling technique. </br>\n<strong>Michelle</strong>: That's exactly what I wanted to tell you, in my company, we realized that UML is great, but it has shortcomings. </br>\n<strong>Jack</strong>: In mine, we're still following it thoroughly, but in this case, it's not working. I have an idea of what I want the software to be like, but following the steps of unified modeling language is leaving some aspects behind. </br>"}, {"time": "38600", "image": "enpe7n4le02ob01re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<strong>Michelle</strong>: I know what you're saying. There are many modeling alternatives available in the industry. However, I had a colleague who tried to use her own modeling, but it created some difficulties in semantics because it wasn't like ours, so we had to \u201ctranslate\u201d what she meant. </br>\n<strong>Jack</strong>: I think that with UML the problem is the same,  sometimes it doesn't allow programmers to explore other alternatives when developing software, and so creativity or dealing with other important elements in a different order might impair the process. </br>"}, {"time": "75000", "image": "enpe7n4le02ob01re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<strong>Michelle</strong>: I see. That reminds me of an occasion when one of my coworkers wanted to focus on the user interface of an application in an early stage, but with UML it wasn't possible. And a friend of mine told me that her company was using UML for business processes! </br>\n<strong>Jack</strong>: Some friends told me they were doing that in theirs too when it's clearly not its purpose. </br>\n<strong>Michelle</strong>: Besides, there are people who would like to have executable UML to save time; that's not going to happen soon. There are so many UML models that it'd be difficult to see all of them in a single software; it would also have to support proprietary models. It's too complex!"}], "coverimg": "enpe7n4le02ob01re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "enpe7n4le02ob01re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can give examples related to UML and different alternatives."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can explain why UML is not sufficient in certain cases."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can describe the cases where UML is not sufficient."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Do you follow modeling languages when writing software? Which one or ones?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Are modeling languages necessary? Why? Why not? "}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "UML: is it good enough?"}], "img_path": "", "id": 0}, {"stimuli_ids": [1], "template_override": 1, "questions": [{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "type": "question"}], "responses": [{"correct": 0, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 0}, {"correct": 1, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 1}], "id": 0}], "type": "STI", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " Two friends are talking about UML."}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Content"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "te